Both \code{simmaps} and \code{densityMaps} objects can be used as inputs for a deepSTRAPP run
with \code{\link[=run_deepSTRAPP_for_focal_time]{run_deepSTRAPP_for_focal_time()}} or \code{\link[=run_deepSTRAPP_over_time]{run_deepSTRAPP_over_time()}}.

\code{simmaps} retain the identity of each simulated history,
allowing deepSTRAPP to keep track of which simulation generated each set of trait values (i.e., states/ranges).
However, retaining all simulated histories can require substantial RAM, particularly for large phylogenies or many simulations.

Alternatively, \code{densityMaps} summarize the frequency of states/ranges across simulations.
